If a patient concurrently uses an opioid-pain-medication and concurrently uses an other-opioid-pain-medication then the patient can have an increased-overdose-risk.
If a patient concurrently uses an opioid-pain-medication and concurrently uses a benzodiazepine then the patient can have an increased-overdose-risk.
If a patient concurrently uses an opioid-pain-medication and concurrently uses some heroin then the patient can have an increased-overdose-risk.
If a patient concurrently uses an opioid-pain-medication and concurrently uses an other-nonpharmaceutical-opioid then the patient can have an increased-overdose-risk.
